        "Rows: 54 (23 on p. 625, 31 on p. 626). Chapter 28 Communications, 'Appendix' at the end of the Shipping section.",
        "Sub-lines '(via Suez Canal)' / '(via Panama Canal)' under Havana, New York and Quebec are printed indented under the port name (which carries no figure of its own); combined into one row each.",
        "p. 625: the figure column is set out of line with the names — in the upper half the figures sit about half a line above the names, and at the foot 13,165 prints level with the 'Havana, Cuba' heading line while nothing prints against 'Karachi, Pakistan'. There are 23 figures for the 23 figure-bearing lines, so they were assigned in order (Havana via Suez 13,165 ... Karachi 5,236). A strictly positional reading would instead leave Hamburg and Karachi blank and shift the Havana-Jinsen figures up one line.",
